  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nUpper ridging over the western U.S. will remain the dominant force\nthe next several days. Extreme Heat warning for Dawson, Prairie\nand Wibaux counties remains in effect through this evening.\nTemperature recovery overnight looks better than last night, so no\nfurther headline planned for Tuesday.  \n\nSatellite showcases a large smoke plume stretched from eastern \nOregon across northern Montana. Smoke will continue to be over \nthe area tonight into Tuesday with unhealthy air quality and \nvariable visibilities. \n\nEnsembles continue to show the hot temperatures continuing for \nseveral days through the weekend with highs in the 90s to around \n100 degrees each day. Conditions will also be dry most of the time with\noccasional shortwave to trigger showers and thunderstorms.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nHigh confidence in the hot weather continuing all week. Low\nconfidence in timing any showers and thunderstorms.\n\nNBM Deviations include HRRR/RAP blends to enhance visibility \nreductions due to smoke.",
